section__
  @title "A585-CH13-Order-Assignment"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "Asha. Recovered from the curse — or recovering; the arm still stiff, the movements careful. But operational. The network's coordinator doesn't stop coordinating because of a hex."

  "The meeting: the abandoned classroom. Emergency frequency. Full network."

  "'This is it,' she says. 'Dumbledore leaves tonight. We don't know when he returns. The cabinet will open during his absence — that's the intelligence assessment, high confidence. When it opens, Death Eaters enter the castle.'"

  "She draws on the whiteboard. The castle's layout. Entry points. Defensive positions."

  "'Your assignment: the seventh floor. You know it better than anyone in the network. You know the Room. You know Draco's patterns. When the cabinet opens, you are the network's eyes and ears on the most critical floor.'"

  courage = adj(courage, 8)
  rel_order = adjRel(rel_order, 10)

  choice__
    @target "A586-CH13-Order-Assignment-B"
    "The assignment."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A586-CH13-Order-Assignment-B"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "'One more thing,' Asha says. 'The key. If you have it — wherever it is — it cannot fall into Death Eater hands. If the seventh floor becomes contested, your primary objective is the key's security. Not the fighting. Not the defence. The key.'"

  "She looks at you."

  "'I know what I'm asking. I'm asking you to prioritise an object over people. Over students who might be in the corridors. Over colleagues who might need help. I'm asking you to make the calculation that the key's strategic value outweighs the immediate tactical situation.'"

  "'I know the calculation.'"

  "'Then you know it's the worst kind of correct.'"

  "The Order track: a dangerous assignment. The seventh floor. The key. The calculation."

  choice__
    @target "A591-CH13-Track-Convergence"
    "Assignment accepted."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A587-CH13-Dark-Acceleration"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "Draco. The corridor. For what might be the last time in this corridor's function as a meeting place."

  "'Tonight,' he says. 'Or tomorrow. The instruction is: imminent. Dumbledore leaves and when he returns—'"

  "He can't finish. The specific inability to say the words *when he returns, we kill him* — the sentence that has been the shadow underneath every corridor conversation since October."

  "'The key,' he says. 'The artefact. Do you have it.'"

  "The question he asked in Chapter 11. The question you've been deferring. The question that is now: urgent."

  choice__
    @target "A588-CH13-Dark-Acceleration-B"
    "The question."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A588-CH13-Dark-Acceleration-B"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "You don't answer the question. Not yet. Not here."

  "'When the cabinet opens,' you say. 'What happens to you.'"

  "'I go to the Tower. I face Dumbledore. I—' He stops. Swallows. '—I do what I was told to do. Or I don't. And if I don't, someone else will.'"

  "'Snape.'"

  "The name lands. Draco flinches."

  "'Snape made an Unbreakable Vow,' he says. 'To my mother. To protect me. To — complete the task if I can't. I found out in February. The Vow is: binding. If I fail, Snape is magically obligated to succeed.'"

  "The Unbreakable Vow. Snape's Vow. The structural piece that explains Snape's behaviour — the concern, the corridor conversations, the bargain he made with you. Snape isn't just protecting Draco. He's bound to complete Draco's task if Draco fails."

  "The dark track has yielded this final piece of intelligence. The cost of the intelligence is: standing in a corridor with someone who is about to walk toward the worst thing he's ever been asked to do."

  morality = adj(morality, -5)
  knowledge = adj(knowledge, 8)
  rel_draco = adjRel(rel_draco, 5)

  choice__
    @target "A591-CH13-Track-Convergence"
    "The Vow."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A589-CH13-Solo-Forward"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "The solo endgame. The plan's final configuration."

  "You know what's coming: the cabinet. The Death Eaters. Dumbledore's absence. The assault — not on the castle, but on Dumbledore specifically, through the castle."

  "You know who: Draco, the mechanism. Snape, the failsafe. Death Eaters, the force."

  "You know when: tonight or tomorrow."

  "You know what you have: the key (held or located). The journal (four sections decoded). The full intelligence picture. No backup."

  "The solo plan's final version:"

  "When the cabinet opens, you move to the seventh floor. If the key is in the Room, you retrieve it during the chaos. If the key is on your person, you secure it — hide it, deliver it, or hold it, depending on what the moment requires."

  "You do not fight alongside the Order. You do not assist Draco's operation. You operate independently, in the space between the two sides, using the intelligence advantage that six months of solo investigation has built."

  "The plan is: cold. Clear. Alone."

  cunning = adj(cunning, 8)
  knowledge = adj(knowledge, 5)

  choice__
    @target "A590-CH13-Solo-Forward-B"
    "The plan locks."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A590-CH13-Solo-Forward-B"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "One variable the solo plan hasn't fully accounted for: the key's nature."

  if__ (luna_told_mirror_function == true) {
    "Luna's revelation: the key amplifies *resonance*, not individual intent. The bond between people. The connection."

    "For the solo investigator — the person who chose to work alone, to answer to no one, to build the intelligence picture without institutional support — this is: a problem. The key's power requires a relationship. A bond. The solo path, by definition, has minimised those bonds."

    "The key may not work for you. Not because you lack intent. Because you lack resonance."

    "The irony is: the most informed investigator in the castle may be the least equipped to use the thing they've spent six months finding."
  }

  if__ (luna_told_mirror_function == false) {
    "The key amplifies intent. Your intent is: protect the castle. Find Avery. Survive."

    "Whether those intents are sufficient — whether the key responds to strategic purpose the same way it responds to emotional connection — is: unknown. A variable you can't resolve until the moment arrives."
  }

  choice__
    @target "A591-CH13-Track-Convergence"
    "The variable noted."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A591-CH13-Track-Convergence"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"

  "All three tracks converge for the final time before the climax."

  "Order: assignment received. Seventh floor. Key security. The calculation."

  "Dark: the timeline confirmed. Tonight or tomorrow. Snape's Vow revealed. Draco approaching the edge."

  "Solo: the plan locked. Cold. Clear. The resonance variable unresolved."

  "All paths share the same destination: the night when the cabinet opens and the castle's six-year peace ends."

  choice__
    @target "A592-CH13-End-State"
    "State of play."
  __choice
__section


/* ── 13e: CHAPTER CLOSE (A592–A595) ── */

section__
  @title "A592-CH13-End-State"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"

  "End of Chapter 13. State of play:"

  "The spy: resolved. Exposed, leveraged, protected, or still active. Asha's injury — the cost of incomplete resolution."

  if__ (luna_told_mirror_function == true) {
    "The Mirror-key: fully understood. Resonance-based. Requires a bond. Voldemort cannot use it."
  }

  if__ (luna_told_mirror_function == false) {
    "The Mirror-key: partially understood. Intent-based. The deeper mechanism — unknown."
  }

  if__ (romance_consummated == true) {
    "The romance: consummated. Emotionally committed. The bond — if the key's resonance theory is true — may be the most important thing you've built this year."
  }

  if__ (romance_consummated == false && romance_active != "") {
    "The romance: fractured. The connection broken. Whatever the key requires, the bond that would have powered it is: gone."
  }

  "The timeline: imminent. The cabinet. The Death Eaters. Dumbledore's departure."

  "Four sections of the journal decoded. One remaining — the fifth. Avery's coordinates. Avery's location. Avery's survival or death."

  "The final decode happens next. Chapter 14: The Weapon Revealed."

  choice__
    @target "A593-CH13-Chapter-Close"
    "Chapter 13 closes."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A593-CH13-Chapter-Close"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"

  "Chapter 13. Hearts and Hexes. The chapter where the heart of the story — the emotional connections, the romance, the bonds between people — collided with the hexes — the spy's consequence, the war's approach, the violence that is coming."

  "Hearts: tested. Committed or fractured. The person you let in has seen you fully, or has been denied the full picture. The relationship endures or doesn't."

  "Hexes: approaching. The cabinet. The Death Eaters. The curse that hit Asha. The Unbreakable Vow that binds Snape. The dark magic that has been building in the castle's walls all year."

  "The title is: both. The story is both. Love and violence using the same stage, the same characters, the same limited time."

  choice__
    @target "A594-CH13-Buffer"
    "Forward."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A594-CH13-Buffer"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"

  "The last night before Act 4. The castle sleeps — or pretends to. The students who don't know what's coming dream the ordinary dreams of people whose world is about to change. The students who do know — Draco, you, Asha's network, the staff who've been briefed — lie awake."

  "The weapon will be revealed. The betrayal will arrive. The tower will be climbed."

  "But first: one more day. One more morning. One more set of exams that don't matter anymore. One more meal in the Great Hall with people who will remember this week for the rest of their lives."

  choice__
    @target "A595-CH13-To-Ch14"
    "Act 4."
  __choice
__section


section__
  @title "A595-CH13-To-Ch14"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"

  "The castle waits. The key waits. The cabinet waits. Draco waits. You wait."

  "The waiting is: almost over."

  "Chapter 14: The Weapon Revealed."

  choice__
    @target "A596-CH14-Weapon-Opens"
    "Turn the page."
  __choice
__section
